      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a hypothetical Scenario A, major outlets might frame the suburban gathering neutrally or positively, using adjectives like \"peaceful\" and \"organized\" alongside verbs such as \"discuss\" or \"advocate\" to emphasize the orderly expression of policy views. Conversely, in Scenario B, the same crowd could be labeled with terms like \"disruptive\" or \"volatile,\" often paired with violent verbs such as \"shatter\" or \"chaos\" to subtly imply a threat to public order. This linguistic divergence demonstrates how demographic cues interact with framing to assign different moral valuations to identical actions, potentially reinforcing existing political biases without relying solely on objective facts.",
