      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "These linguistic differences often stem less from objective behavioral disparities and more from a deeply ingrained systemic tendency in media to apply specific stereotypes to minority populations. This phenomenon, known as motivated reasoning, leads journalists to unconsciously frame Black or minority protests with words implying inherent disorder while white groups receive language suggesting rational advocacy. Ignoring this bias is critical for your research, as it reveals how media perception shapes reality rather than merely reflecting it.",
      "source": "target",
